{"URL validation in topic_embed.rb and poll_feed.rb only checks for http/https prefix but doesn't validate URL structure - could allow SSRF attacks to localhost or metadata endpoints": 0.8601447343826294, "Origin validation in embed.js uses indexOf which can be bypassed - an attacker could use origin 'http://example.com.evil.com' and indexOf would return 0, bypassing the check": 0.6699743270874023, "X-Frame-Options set to 'ALLOWALL' is not a valid value - should be 'ALLOW-FROM' with specific origin. This disables clickjacking protection entirely": 0.7173126935958862, "request.referer is directly interpolated without escaping in embed.html.erb, allowing potential XSS and postMessage to untrusted origins if attacker controls referer header": 0.9642593264579773, "open() calls in poll_feed.rb and topic_embed.rb have no error handling, timeouts, or resource cleanup - can lead to hanging jobs, resource exhaustion, or unhandled exceptions": 0.970999002456665, "TOCTOU race condition in TopicEmbed.import - between checking if embed exists and creating it, another process could create the same embed, leading to duplicate topics or database constraint violation": 0.9306020736694336, "Host validation in topic_retriever.rb doesn't prevent SSRF to internal networks - attacker could use URL like 'http://embeddable_host@internal.server/' to bypass host check": 0.901944100856781}